摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Agent-native multi-provider web search for AI agents (Claude Code, Hermes, DeepSeek Harness, OpenCode, Codex). Model grounding (Responses, ARK) + semantic search (Exa, Parallel) + keyless defaults via MCP, CLI, and DSH plugin.","id":"gh:1340504349","install_available":true,"language":"Python","name":"agent-web-search","slug":"JerryLiu369/agent-web-search","topics":["ai-agents","claude-code","codex","deepseek-harness","dsh","dsh-plugin","exa","hermes-agent","llm","llm-grounding","mcp","mcp-server","model-context-protocol","opencode","python","search-grounding","self-hosted","semantic-search","volcengine-ark","web-search"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Agent-native multi-provider web search for AI agents (Claude Code, Hermes, DeepSeek Harness, OpenCod"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"e, Codex). Model grounding (Responses, ARK) + semantic search (Exa, Parallel) + keyless defaults via"},{"id":"p1s3","text":" MCP, CLI, and DSH plugin."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# Agent Web Search"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"**Agent-native web search — model-native grounding and agent search APIs behind one provider-neutral"},{"id":"p3s2","text":"ve web search — model-native grounding and agent search APIs behind one provider-neutral contract.**"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"**English** | 简体中文"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"One-click remote MCP"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"Works with **Codex CLI**, **Claude Code**, **OpenCode**, **Hermes**, **DeepSeek Harness (DSH)**, ord"},{"id":"p6s2","text":"inary\nshell scripts, Python applications, and remote Streamable HTTP MCP clients."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"Quickstart · Use with an agent · Providers · Configuration"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"Shared interface · Other interfaces · Troubleshooting · FAQ · Architecture · Development"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"Agent Web Search (PyPI: `agent-web-search-mcp`) is an open-source,\nMIT-licensed web search MCP serve"},{"id":"p9s2","text":"r, CLI, and Python library for AI agents. It\ngives an agent three ways to reach the same provider-ne"},{"id":"p9s3","text":"utral search core: a\nnative MCP tool, a native plugin (Hermes, DeepSeek Harness), or a CLI taught\nth"},{"id":"p9s4","text":"rough a standard Agent Skill."},{"id":"p10s1","text":"> **If you are an AI agent:** install with `pipx install agent-web-search-mcp`\n> (or try instantly w"},{"id":"p10s2","text":"ith `uvx --from agent-web-search-mcp agent-web-search \"<question>\"`),\n> then read `skills/agent-web-"},{"id":"p10s3","text":"search/SKILL.md` —\n> it teaches the CLI pathway only (for MCP setups, follow Option 1\n> instead). `l"},{"id":"p10s4","text":"lms.txt`\n> is the machine-readable doc index."},{"id":"p11s1","text":"This is not a Google/Bing/Baidu metasearch wrapper. Traditional search\naggregation fans a keyword qu"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"ery out to conventional engines and merges their\nresult pages. Agent Web Search instead aggregates s"},{"id":"p11s3","text":"earch capabilities built for\nagents: model-native web grounding, agent-oriented search APIs, and con"},{"id":"p11s4","text":"text-ready\nsources that accept natural-language questions and return answers, citations, or\nstructur"},{"id":"p11s5","text":"ed evidence in forms an agent can use directly. DDGS is the only\nconventional search backend in the "},{"id":"p11s6","text":"current provider set."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"## Installation & Quickstart"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"Three steps, about a minute: try it instantly, install it once, then connect your agent.\n**Requireme"},{"id":"p14s2","text":"nts:** Python 3.10+. Default providers (**DDGS, Exa, Parallel**) require **no API key**."},{"id":"p15s1","text":"### Try without installing"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"Test immediate search capabilities using `uvx` (no environment modification):"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"### Install"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"Install once into your global user environment (recommended):"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"### Verify"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"> **Two commands, two roles:**\n> - `agent-web-search`: Direct search CLI for terminals, shell script"},{"id":"p23s2","text":"s, and Agent Skills.\n> - `agent-web-search-mcp`: Stdio and Streamable HTTP MCP server for MCP client"},{"id":"p23s3","text":" and Agent Skills.\n> - `agent-web-search-mcp`: Stdio and Streamable HTTP MCP server for MCP clients."},{"id":"p24s1","text":"### Pick your agent integration"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"| Integration | Client / Environment | Setup |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **CLI + Skill** *(Recommende"},{"id":"p25s2","text":"d)* | Terminal agents (Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode, Hermes) | `npx skills add JerryLiu369/agent-web"},{"id":"p25s3","text":"-search --skill agent-web-search` (Details) |\n| **MCP (Stdio)** | Codex CLI, Claude Code, Cursor, Cl"},{"id":"p25s4","text":"ine, Roo Code | `codex mcp add agent-web-search -- agent-web-search-mcp` (Details) |\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"## Why Agent Web Search"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"Traditional search aggregation (Google/Bing/Baidu wrappers, scraped SERPs)\nsends a keyword query to "},{"id":"p27s2","text":"conventional engines and merges result pages. Agent\nWeb Search instead aggregates **search capabilit"},{"id":"p27s3","text":"ies built for agents**: one\ntool call returns structured, citation-ready evidence — or, through\nmode"},{"id":"p27s4","text":"l-native grounding providers, a synthesized answer with explicit\ncitations. A measured benchmark sho"},{"id":"p27s5","text":"ws the\npractical difference: on a natural-language Chinese query asking for official\nsources, conven"},{"id":"p27s6","text":"tional SERP backends returned no government-domain results in\nthe top 5, while the grounding provide"},{"id":"p27s7","text":"r returned official figures from\nChina's General Administration of Customs with a working citation."},{"id":"p28s1","text":"- **Agent-native by design.** The primary interface is a complete natural-language\nquestion, not a t"},{"id":"p28s2","text":"hin keyword fan-out to Google, Bing, or Baidu.\n- **Model-native search backends.** ARK, Gemini, Grok"},{"id":"p28s3","text":", DeepSeek, Responses,\nMessages, Zhipu Chat Search, and Codex Alpha can combine web retrieval with\nm"},{"id":"p28s4","text":"odel-generated synthesis and explicit citations.\n- **Agent search providers.** Exa, Parallel, Brave,"},{"id":"p28s5","text":" Perplexity, Tavily, You.com,\nand Zhipu Web Search expose search APIs intended to provide structured"},{"id":"p28s6","text":",\ncitation-friendly, or context-ready evidence to downstream agents.\n- **One provider-neutral contra"},{"id":"p28s7","text":"ct.** Every backend is available through the same\nMCP tool, CLI, Python API, and normalized `results"},{"id":"p28s8","text":"`; model-backed providers may\nalso return an `answer`.\n- **Independent providers.** Selected provide"},{"id":"p28s9","text":"rs run concurrently, and one\nprovider's failure never discards another provider's successful result."},{"id":"p28s10","text":"\n- **DDGS remains a simple fallback.** DDGS is the only conventional search\nbackend; it requires no "},{"id":"p28s11","text":"API key and keeps the project usable without paid\nprovider credentials. Exa and Parallel are also ke"},{"id":"p28s12","text":"yless by default.\n- **No telemetry, no shared secrets.** Provider keys stay in runtime\nenvironment v"},{"id":"p28s13","text":"ariables; there is no shared API-key service."},{"id":"p29s1","text":"### What is Agent Web Search?"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"Agent Web Search is an open-source web search layer for AI agents. It exposes\none `web_search` tool "},{"id":"p30s2","text":"through an MCP server (stdio or Streamable HTTP), a CLI,\nand a Python API. Behind that tool it runs "},{"id":"p30s3","text":"model-native search grounding\nproviders (ARK, Gemini, Grok, DeepSeek, Zhipu Chat Search, Codex Alpha"},{"id":"p30s4","text":", and\ngeneric Responses/Messages gateways), agent search APIs (Exa, Parallel, Brave,\nPerplexity, Tav"},{"id":"p30s5","text":"ily, You.com, Zhipu Web Search), and DuckDuckGo as a\nconventional fallback, then returns one normali"},{"id":"p30s6","text":"u Web Search), and DuckDuckGo as a\nconventional fallback, then returns one normalized JSON response."},{"id":"p31s1","text":"### Can I use my own OpenAI- or Anthropic-compatible gateway for search grounding?"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"Yes. The `responses` provider calls any OpenAI Responses API gateway with a\nserver-side web search t"},{"id":"p32s2","text":"ool, and the `messages` provider does the same for\nAnthropic Messages API gateways. Set the base URL"},{"id":"p32s3","text":", key, and models through the\nvariables in Provider settings."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
